-- title:
--   Two-chart pole datum from a section of 𝒪(mε)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a local Noetherian commutative ring, let $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a proper morphism of schemes that is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity. Let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number and let $s$ be a morphism from the unit object of the category of $C$-modules to `(ε.1.ker ^ m).invModule`, the dual of the module attached to the $m$-th power of the ideal sheaf data of $\varepsilon$ — that is, a global section of $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon)$. Assume that no point in the image of $\varepsilon$ lies in the support of `Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal s`, the least ideal sheaf datum whose ideal on each affine open $U$ contains the ideal generated by the coefficients of $s$ on $U$. Then there exist opens $U, V \subseteq C$ covering $C$, with $U$ exactly the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, and sections $f \in \Gamma(C,U)$, $g \in \Gamma(C,V)$ such that $U \cap V$ equals both the basic open of $f$ and the basic open of $g$, the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U \cap V$ have product $1$, and moreover: for the $R$-algebra structure on $\Gamma(C,V)$ induced by $c$, the quotient $\Gamma(C,V)/(g)$ is a free $R$-module of rank $m$; and for every field $K$ with an $R$-algebra structure, the image of $f$ (respectively of $g$) under pullback along the base change $C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} K \to C$, viewed in the sections over the preimage of $U$ (respectively $V$) with its $K$-algebra structure, is transcendental over $K$.
--
--   This packages the classical construction of a two-chart presentation of a smooth proper relative curve from a section of $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon)$ with zero scheme disjoint from $\varepsilon$: $U$ is the complement of the section, $V$ the complement of the zero scheme, and $f$, $g$ are the two reciprocal trivialising coordinates, with $\Gamma(C,V)/(g)$ the ring of the $m$-th infinitesimal neighbourhood of $\varepsilon$. It feeds the construction of the two-affine-open cover of such a curve and of the associated pole datum with transcendence and unit conditions.
-- source:
